<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43363" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sē-grex</span></b> , ĕgis
		(collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēgrĕgus</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Aus.
			Parent. 8, 10</span></i>), adj.
		grex, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>apart</i>, <i>separate</i> (post-Aug. and mostly
				<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agere vitam segregem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ben. 4, 18, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">segregem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Hippol. 1208</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">civitates situ segreges,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 9, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Prud. Cath. 7, 28</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">segrege formā,</span>”
				i. e. <i>different</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ham. 804</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">segrege regno,</span>”
				<i>divided</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 66</span></i>
			.</div>
